{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-ba410d77cff741d8", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787750421.1898057, "trigger_id": "trg-0d2c5d23220a5f049021ba3e", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "Health Catalyst is a Nasdaq-listed healthcare data-and-analytics company (a leading provider of data and analytics technology and services to healthcare organizations) that has been deepening its AI strategy through a Microsoft partnership, acquiring patient engagement company Upfront Healthcare Services, and introducing new AI-integrated analytics offerings. Its core product positioning — using AI to identify which interventions are most likely to move outcomes like length of stay, readmissions, and mortality — places it squarely in the \"AI assembles evidence, human decides\" design space that our post argues is the only defensible posture right now. That distinction matters urgently because the WISeR controversy has put the entire industry on notice: physician groups and members of Congress have expressed concern about WISeR's potential impact on provider workloads and beneficiary access, particularly as health technology partners are rewarded based, in part, on the volume of care they deny. Health Catalyst's provider-organization client base is directly affected — their customers must now demonstrate not just AI accuracy, but governance: the audit trail, the human oversight checkpoints, and the documented policies that connect AI output to a named, accountable process. Health Catalyst has publicly flagged that limitations of black-box software have severely hampered AI's effectiveness for healthcare organizations, which aligns with the post's argument for transparency. The open question for a first conversation: **As Health Catalyst embeds more AI into clinical and financial workflows for provider clients, how are you thinking about building the governance layer — audit trails, human-in-the-loop checkpoints, explainability — into those products before regulators or a client's board asks to see it?**", "event_id": "1282435670", "object_id": "533990588137", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
