{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-5c8f1d1292164aaa", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787750469.6129985, "trigger_id": "trg-0c5309d5542f56fdbe2cef8e", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "Innovaccer is a healthcare AI company whose Gravity platform sits squarely in the eye of the storm the WISeR post describes. Gravity is Innovaccer's healthcare-native AI platform — it unifies clinical, claims, financial, and operational data and deploys AI agents that execute operational work such as prior authorization, care gap outreach, enrollment, and scheduling with configurable human oversight at every step. That design philosophy maps almost exactly onto the post's \"defensible architecture\" argument. Innovaccer's own technical documentation notes that when an agent submits a prior auth, a compliance team needs to be able to trace what data the agent saw, what logic it applied, what action it took, and what human reviewed it — calling demonstrable auditability a core deployment requirement. Gravity also incorporates a configurable human-in-the-loop governance model, allowing providers to review, modify, or approve AI-generated outputs before decisions are finalized. Meanwhile, Innovaccer was recognized by Black Book Research as the top-ranked vendor in both AI-Powered Revenue Cycle Autonomy and Population Health Data Integration for 2026, with dual recognition underscoring its leadership in autonomous, agentic AI for healthcare. The WISeR controversy — centering on whether AI drives a denial versus assembles evidence for a human — is a direct governance question for any platform selling autonomous prior-auth agents at scale. The opening question for a rep: *As Innovaccer scales Gravity's agentic prior-auth capabilities across more health system customers, how are you currently handling the explainability and audit-trail requirements that CMS and payers are increasingly scrutinizing in the wake of the WISeR backlash?*", "event_id": "147976899", "object_id": "534035230400", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
