{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-6ee29c9b374f4893", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787751504.7083004, "trigger_id": "trg-344214815c5554aabefd8130", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "Health Catalyst (Nasdaq: HCAT) is a leading provider of data and analytics technology and services to healthcare organizations, and the company has been executing an aggressive AI pivot: it forged an AI partnership with Microsoft, acquired patient engagement company Upfront Healthcare Services, and introduced new AI-integrated analytics offerings. Health Catalyst uses AI to identify which interventions are most likely to move outcomes like length of stay, readmissions, and mortality before teams invest time and effort — positioning its AI squarely in the evidence-assembly role rather than the decision-rendering role. That distinction is now politically and legally charged: Congressional Democrats introduced a CRA resolution in May 2026 to repeal CMS's WISeR model, which uses AI and ML to streamline prior authorization for Traditional Medicare, with the core objection being lack of governance, not model accuracy. Only 22% of hospital leaders surveyed in late 2025 were highly confident they could produce a 30-day AI audit trail for regulators or payers — a gap that directly implicates any vendor, like Health Catalyst, whose AI-powered insights feed clinical and financial decisions at provider organizations. Limitations of black-box software and an overly narrow focus on predictive models have severely hampered AI's effectiveness for healthcare organizations — a challenge Health Catalyst itself acknowledges. Given Health Catalyst's role as the analytics layer underpinning decisions at provider clients, the question worth opening with is: **How is Health Catalyst currently thinking about embedding human-in-the-loop controls and audit trails into the AI-driven insights it delivers to provider organizations, so those clients can demonstrate governance to regulators and payers?**", "event_id": "3249332950", "object_id": "533990588137", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
