{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-f3e87d755b244d39", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787751531.8848593, "trigger_id": "trg-a0edc4b0dd03506fb3bb92a2", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "**lead_context — Mahesh Venkatagiri, VP, Accolade (now Transcarent)**\n\nSince April 2025, Accolade has operated as part of Transcarent following a $621M merger, with the combined organization now serving more than 20 million members and 1,700 employer and health plan clients. The integration's central bet is AI: Transcarent blends its AI-powered WayFinding navigation system with Accolade's True Health Actions platform to deliver personalized care guidance drawn from employer data, health plans, and electronic health records. Transcarent integrates AI into its affiliated virtual clinic to gather relevant history and symptoms before visits, structuring inputs for the clinician to review — explicitly positioning AI as reducing administrative burden so clinicians can focus on diagnosis and care planning. That design philosophy — AI assembling evidence for a human who retains the decision — maps directly to the governance distinction our post draws against WISeR. The WISeR controversy is now a settled cautionary reference point: the Senate voted 46–50 on July 16, 2026 to keep WISeR in place, but the close vote and the debate it generated have put AI-assisted care decisions firmly under congressional and regulatory scrutiny. States are also leading in 2026, enacting laws that govern insurers' use of AI in prior authorization, increase transparency requirements, and require human oversight for adverse determinations. As a VP at a platform that is actively scaling agentic AI across 20M+ members, Mahesh is squarely in the audience for this governance conversation. A good opening question: *As Transcarent scales WayFinding's agentic AI features across Accolade's member base, what does your current audit and human-oversight architecture look like for decisions that could influence a member's care path?*", "event_id": "4203571807", "object_id": "533994194677", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
