{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-e066a9285cd049fa", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787751556.2753234, "trigger_id": "trg-cbfc1107a67858daad85ba19", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "Innovaccer sits squarely at the intersection of the WISeR governance controversy. Its flagship Gravity platform unifies clinical, financial, and operational data and deploys AI agents to execute work across workflows, and is specifically designed to support AI orchestration, governance, and auditability so organizations can scale automation beyond isolated pilots. That design philosophy is directly relevant: Gravity agents handle prior authorization, care gap outreach, and scheduling with configurable human oversight at every workflow node — precisely the human-in-the-loop architecture the post argues is the defensible alternative to WISeR-style black-box decision rendering. Risant Health reportedly reduced prior authorization time from about 45 minutes to less than a minute using Innovaccer's agentic AI, a headline result that now carries regulatory risk if the governance story isn't airtight. Gravity markets audit-ready workflows across risk, quality, and utilization management, with support for CMS-aligned prior authorization turnaround and reporting, and transparent AI with human oversight — claims the WISeR backlash will put under a sharper spotlight. The Senate has already rejected the Democrat-led CRA resolution, but the political scrutiny on AI-driven prior authorization has not dissipated, and any vendor deploying agents in that workflow will face customer and regulatory pressure to demonstrate the governance layer concretely. **Opening question for the rep:** As Innovaccer scales Gravity's prior authorization agents across more health systems, how are they documenting and surfacing the human-review step in a way that would satisfy a CMS auditor or a skeptical congressional inquiry?", "event_id": "3610415997", "object_id": "534035230400", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
