{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-90201a66b37e41dd", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787751581.5892432, "trigger_id": "trg-b80a9e2fcdc453bbbcced505", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "Axiom Law sits at the precise intersection of this post's concerns. As a global alternative legal services provider serving 75% of the Fortune 100 with 3,000+ engagements annually, Axiom has a live stake in the AI governance debate — both as a deployer of AI in legal workflows and as a supplier of legal talent to healthcare clients navigating that same debate. Shared client results in healthcare show that Axiom's combination of Legora's AI and vetted legal talent is already delivering faster turnarounds and cost savings for in-house legal teams managing high-volume work. The WISeR controversy is directly relevant to those healthcare clients: the Senate voted in July 2026 to keep the AI-assisted prior-authorization pilot in place, defeating a CRA repeal 46–50, but the governance questions it surfaced — human review, audit trails, transparency — have not gone away. States are actively enacting laws in 2026 requiring transparency, human oversight, and accountability for adverse AI determinations in healthcare. Meanwhile, Axiom's own 2026 In-House Legal AI Report acknowledges that legal AI is widespread but execution lags, with governance as the gap. Axiom's 2025 AI study found that only 20% of legal departments achieve AI maturity despite 33% budget increases — a competency gap that maps squarely onto the ungoverned-AI risk the post describes. **Opening question for a first call:** Given that Axiom is both deploying AI in its own delivery model and advising healthcare clients whose legal teams must now respond to a rapidly expanding patchwork of state AI-governance mandates, how is Axiom currently helping those in-house teams distinguish between AI that drives decisions versus AI that assembles evidence for a human reviewer — and where does that line sit in Axiom's own tools?", "event_id": "421723885", "object_id": "533963448020", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
