{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-8cd300b9836b4e46", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787755419.2997355, "trigger_id": "trg-1a5f81f2d2b957f18a3faef8", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "Health Catalyst is a Nasdaq-listed healthcare data and analytics company whose core platform, Ignite Intelligence, combines shared models, AI agents, benchmarks, and comparison services — with flagship offerings like Clinical Cost Intelligence using ML-driven variation analysis and LLM-enabled opportunity screening to deliver insights at scale. The company recently sold its Vitalware revenue-cycle business for $147 million, explicitly to sharpen focus on AI, analytics, and its core technology platform, and plans to use proceeds to repay ~$160 million in debt — giving it greater flexibility to invest in AI-driven innovation. This strategic pivot means Health Catalyst's engineering and product teams are almost certainly building or expanding Python-based API services powering these AI analytics pipelines. The Apitally post speaks directly to this context: logging is critical for production FastAPI apps, and for APIs it breaks down into request logs — recording individual requests and responses — and application logs from the application's code. By default Apitally doesn't capture sensitive data, making it suitable for environments with strict privacy requirements — a non-trivial point for a company handling hundreds of millions of patient records under HIPAA. The one question a rep could open with: **\"As Health Catalyst doubles down on its AI analytics platform after the Vitalware divestiture, how is the engineering team currently handling observability and request-level logging for the FastAPI services powering Ignite?\"**", "event_id": "303472296", "object_id": "533990588137", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
