{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-0fcd289219164a64", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787755447.0955997, "trigger_id": "trg-5a4ab2aebd9353ee8ac8c5d7", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "**lead_context — Mahesh Venkatagiri, VP, Accolade / Transcarent**\n\nAccolade was acquired by Transcarent in April 2025 for $621 million and is now an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary operating under the Transcarent brand. The combined organization serves over 20 million members and more than 1,700 employer and health plan clients. The technical integration work is substantial: Transcarent is blending its AI-powered WayFinding navigation system with Accolade's True Health Actions platform, drawing on employer data, health plans, and electronic health records. The combined organization is also integrating Accolade's Trusted Partner Ecosystem and Transcarent's provider relationships within a unified Experience Store, offering point solutions across mental health, diabetes, fertility, musculoskeletal care, and more — all through a secure platform with single sign-on integration. In January 2026, Transcarent announced major new agentic capabilities added to its WayFinding platform at CES. This post-merger integration phase — two distinct API-heavy platforms being unified at speed — makes API observability acutely relevant: logging is critical for understanding and debugging FastAPI apps in production, and for APIs specifically, it breaks down into request logs and application logs, with logs being the best starting point when things go wrong. For a VP overseeing engineering or product at this newly merged entity, the central question is likely how to maintain visibility across previously separate systems now being stitched together. **Opening question for the rep:** As Accolade's platform gets integrated into Transcarent's stack, how is the team currently handling API-level observability across systems that weren't originally built to talk to each other?", "event_id": "615421925", "object_id": "533994194677", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
