{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-93017eb9e824445b", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787755469.8655987, "trigger_id": "trg-f64427bbe64d537f80bf9b20", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "Innovaccer is one of the most active builders of agentic AI in healthcare right now. The company was named a Leader in the inaugural 2026 Gartner Magic Quadrant for Healthcare Provider Industry Cloud Platforms, and was recognized as the top-ranked vendor in both AI-Powered Revenue Cycle Autonomy and Population Health Data Integration by Black Book Research in 2026. Underpinning all of this is Gravity, a cloud-agnostic data and AI infrastructure layer that ingests and normalizes data from EHR systems, claims, pharmacy, labs, remote monitoring, and social determinants of health. Innovaccer is committing $250 million to expand this AI agent platform, which automates workflows across prior authorization, revenue cycle management, and population health. That scale of agentic API surface area — spanning clinical, operational, and financial workflows — makes API observability a genuine operational concern: logging is critical for understanding and debugging applications in production, and for APIs specifically it breaks down into request logs and application logs, both of which matter when things go wrong. Apitally by default doesn't capture sensitive data, making it suitable for environments with strict privacy requirements — directly relevant for a healthcare platform handling PHI at enterprise scale. A good opening question for a rep: **As Innovaccer scales its Gravity platform to power more autonomous agents across health system workflows, how are your engineering teams currently maintaining visibility into API performance and errors across that growing surface area?**", "event_id": "750612594", "object_id": "534035230400", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
