{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-5e0130fde229414d", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787755498.77269, "trigger_id": "trg-2eddbadc2d6850669f132c7a", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "⚠️ **Important mismatch flagged before writing the note.**\n\nThe published post (https://apitally.io/blog/fastapi-logging-guide) is a **developer-focused technical guide** about setting up request logging and application log correlation in **FastAPI (a Python web framework)**. Its themes are: API observability, structured logging, debugging in production, and request/response traceability.\n\n**Axiom Law** is a global **alternative legal services provider** — they supply on-demand lawyers to in-house legal departments. There is no evidence from search results that Axiom Law builds or operates FastAPI applications, employs software engineers in an API-development capacity, or has any connection to the technical themes of the Apitally post. The industry tag on the lead is \"HEALTHCARE,\" but Axiom Law is a legal services company that *serves* healthcare clients — it is not itself a healthcare company, nor a software/engineering company.\n\nThis means **the post and the lead do not match**: the post targets engineering teams building Python APIs, while the lead is the President of a legal talent marketplace. There is no meaningful bridge between FastAPI logging and Axiom Law's business that would make for honest, grounded outreach.\n\n---\n\n**lead_context note (written at industry level as instructed, flagging the mismatch):**\n\n---\n\nAxiom Law is a global alternative legal services provider, not a software engineering organization, making the connection to a FastAPI logging guide tenuous. Axiom delivers on-demand legal talent, secondments, and AI-enabled legal services to in-house legal departments, and serves 75% of the Fortune 100 with over 3,000 engagements annually across six regions. Their healthcare vertical is active: shared client results across healthcare, aerospace, real estate, and manufacturing show that Axiom's combination of AI-enabled legal talent is delivering faster turnarounds and significant cost savings for in-house legal teams managing high-volume legal work. Specifically, Axiom deployed an AI-enabled senior lawyer who used Legora to process 344 supplier contracts for a Fortune 10 healthcare company, migrating hundreds of agreements ahead of a product launch. Axiom now offers 850+ AI-experienced legal professionals, but their own 2025 AI study reveals only 20% of legal departments achieve AI maturity despite 33% budget increases. The post's themes — API observability, structured logging, and request traceability — do not map naturally to Axiom Law's business model. **Recommend verifying whether the lead was correctly matched to this post before outreach.** If outreach proceeds, the one question a rep could open with is: *As Axiom scales its AI Tech+Talent platform to handle high-volume legal workflows for healthcare clients, what does your engineering or product team's approach to monitoring and auditing the APIs that underpin those AI services look like today?*", "event_id": "3804755555", "object_id": "533963448020", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
