{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-c216c9379c3a40df", "event": "run_summary", "ts": 1787757020.3921177, "trigger_id": null, "events_received": 1, "routed": 1, "discarded": 0, "routing_errors": 0, "discards_by_reason": {}, "dispatched_ok": 1, "dispatched_failed": 0, "duration_ms": 4206.91}
{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-b70129b2e86d44cb", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787757042.359574, "trigger_id": "trg-9f29cc2c8ee15219b0106810", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "I now have enough information to write the lead_context note. Let me synthesize everything.\n\n**lead_context note:**\n\n---\n\nMahesh Venkatagiri holds a VP-level role at what was Accolade — now fully absorbed into Transcarent following a $621 million merger completed in April 2025. The combined organization serves over 20 million members and more than 1,700 employer and health plan clients. The integration ambition is explicitly technology-forward: the platform brings together Transcarent's AI-powered WayFinding with Accolade's True Health Actions, delivering clinical guidance personalized for each member. That scale of integration — merging two separately built, API-heavy digital health platforms — makes backend observability a live operational problem, not an academic one. Logging is critical for understanding and debugging FastAPI apps in production; when things go wrong, logs are the best starting point, covering both request logs and application logs, ideally correlated so each log record is linked to the API request that triggered it. For a newly merged platform handling member care navigation at this volume, gaps in request-level visibility translate directly into degraded member experience and slower incident response. Apitally by default doesn't capture any sensitive data, making it suitable for environments with strict privacy requirements — a meaningful differentiator in regulated healthcare. Opening question for a first conversation: *When your engineering team is troubleshooting an incident across the merged Accolade/Transcarent API stack today, how quickly can they correlate a failing member request back to the specific service log that caused it?*", "event_id": "2160093537", "object_id": "533994194677", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
