{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-6300eadf6d0246f2", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787757090.6208918, "trigger_id": "trg-8e870fb4c67550a5bde98a15", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "That said, here is the most honest and useful note I can write, staying at the industry level where the connection is weakest and flagging the mismatch plainly:\n\n---\n\n**lead_context — Mahesh Puliganti, President, Axiom Law**\n\nThe post-to-lead match here is weak and should be noted upfront: the published piece is a technical developer guide on FastAPI request logging and API observability — a software engineering topic. Axiom Law is not a software company; it is an alternative legal services provider. That said, Axiom is deeply invested in AI-enabled delivery right now: Axiom and Legora marked one year of their AI Tech+Talent partnership in June 2026, with shared client results across healthcare, aerospace, and other sectors showing faster turnarounds and significant cost savings. Axiom now fields 850+ AI-experienced legal professionals, and its own 2025 AI study found that only 20% of legal departments achieve AI maturity despite 33% budget increases. In healthcare specifically, Axiom deployed an AI-enabled senior lawyer to process 344 supplier contracts for a Fortune 10 healthcare company, saving 70% compared to outside counsel costs. The most honest angle for outreach is not logging per se, but the broader observability and governance question that underlies it: as Axiom scales AI-assisted legal work for healthcare clients — who face strict HIPAA and regulatory data requirements — how does Axiom ensure visibility, auditability, and control over what its AI tools are doing with sensitive data at the API/workflow level? Opening question for the rep: *As Axiom expands AI-enabled delivery to healthcare clients with strict data governance requirements, what does your current approach look like for auditing and monitoring the AI workflows handling that sensitive legal and clinical data?*", "event_id": "4019666734", "object_id": "533963448020", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
