{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-6efbc366d8714f02", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787757217.0175238, "trigger_id": "trg-105571249fab562c85f6bce6", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "**The post** ([apitally.io/blog/fastapi-logging-guide](https://apitally.io/blog/fastapi-logging-guide)) is a **software engineering / API monitoring guide** — it covers request logs, which record individual API requests and responses, and application logs, which contain detailed messages from application code, aimed at developers building and debugging Python/FastAPI applications in production.\n\n**The lead** — Mahesh Puliganti, President of Axiom Law — sits in the **alternative legal services industry**, not software engineering. Axiom is a global alternative legal services provider delivering on-demand legal talent, secondments, and AI-enabled legal services to in-house legal departments; founded in 2000, it today serves 75% of the Fortune 100, with 3,000+ engagements annually across six regions globally. There is no public evidence that Axiom Law builds or operates FastAPI-based developer tooling.\n\nThe post's themes (FastAPI request logging, structured log output, production debugging) do not map naturally to what Axiom Law does or buys. The industry tag \"HEALTHCARE\" on the lead likely refers to Axiom's *healthcare vertical*, not a shared technical context with the post.\n\nThat said, here is the best-effort `lead_context` note, grounding only what the search supports:\n\n---\n\n**lead_context:**\n\nAxiom Law is a global alternative legal services provider whose healthcare vertical places vetted lawyers with in-house legal departments across compliance, fraud and abuse, and health IT matters. The company has been investing heavily in AI-enabled delivery: Axiom now offers 850+ AI-experienced legal professionals, helping in-house teams boost efficiency with vetted AI tools and expert legal talent, and its partnership with agentic AI platform Legora is producing shared client results across healthcare, including faster turnarounds and significant cost savings for high-volume legal work. Axiom's own 2025 AI study found that only 20% of legal departments achieve AI maturity despite 33% budget increases, a gap Axiom is actively positioning itself to close for clients — and presumably managing internally too. As Axiom scales its AI Tech+Talent services, the observability, logging, and auditability of the underlying APIs and tooling those lawyers depend on becomes operationally critical — which is where our FastAPI logging guide is most relevant. **Opening question:** As Axiom expands its AI-enabled legal delivery for healthcare clients, how is the engineering or legal-ops team currently handling visibility and auditability into the API workflows powering those AI tools?\n\n---\n\n> **Note to email agent:** The thematic connection here is indirect — the post speaks to software teams, but Axiom is a legal services firm. The angle to pursue is Axiom's internal or partner engineering teams who build/maintain the AI legal tooling, not Puliganti's legal practice itself. Confirm whether there is a CTO or engineering contact before drafting outreach to the President.", "event_id": "3986992408", "object_id": "533963448020", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
