{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-4f12e7cacb0e4392", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787758037.869266, "trigger_id": "trg-86f50ffc69945f90b142296c", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "That said, here is the most honest and grounded research note possible, staying at the industry level where the connection fails at the company level:\n\n---\n\n**lead_context note for Mahesh Puliganti, President, Axiom Law**\n\nThe post linked for this outreach is a technical developer guide on configuring logging and observability for FastAPI Python APIs — a software engineering topic with no evident thematic overlap with Axiom Law's core business or the healthcare legal services industry. No connection can be responsibly constructed without fabricating one. What is well-documented about Axiom is directly relevant context regardless: shared client results across healthcare, aerospace, real estate, and manufacturing show that Axiom's combination of AI-enabled legal talent and agentic AI is delivering faster turnarounds, cleaner data, and significant cost savings for in-house legal teams managing high-volume legal work. A notable recent example involved deploying an AI-enabled senior lawyer to process 344 supplier contracts for a Fortune 10 healthcare company, with the client saving 70% compared to outside counsel costs. Axiom's own 2025 AI study found that only 20% of legal departments achieve AI maturity despite 33% budget increases, pointing to dangerous competency gaps across the legal sector — a tension Puliganti, as President, is likely navigating directly with healthcare clients. A strong opening question for a rep: *Given that Axiom's healthcare clients are already seeing 70% cost savings on AI-assisted contract work, how is Puliganti thinking about scaling that model to address the broader AI maturity gap he's seeing across his healthcare in-house team engagements?*\n\n---\n\n**⚠️ Flagging for the email agent:** The published post (`apitally.io/blog/fastapi-logging-guide`) covers FastAPI API logging — a purely technical software topic. It does not map to legal services, healthcare compliance, AI governance in law, or any theme relevant to Axiom Law. The email agent should **not** attempt to reference this post in outreach to this lead, or should request the correct post before drafting.", "event_id": "364306365", "object_id": "533963448020", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
