{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-7faf35c484714ffd", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787758452.7428467, "trigger_id": "trg-1edb32ffdcd05f44947f16f6", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "I'll write an honest note that flags this mismatch clearly, grounds what *is* known about Axiom Law in healthcare, and gives the rep an accurate picture — rather than fabricating a forced connection.\n\n---\n\n**lead_context — Mahesh Puliganti, President, Axiom Law**\n\n⚠️ **Relevance gap to flag:** The published post (Apitally's FastAPI logging guide) is a developer-facing technical article about API request logging and observability tooling. Axiom Law is not a software engineering organization building APIs — it is an alternative legal services provider. No credible connection between FastAPI logging and Axiom Law's work was found; any link would be fabricated. What *is* well-documented: Axiom and Legora marked one year of their AI Tech+Talent partnership in June 2026, with shared client results across healthcare, aerospace, and real estate showing faster turnarounds and significant cost savings for in-house legal teams. In one notable healthcare engagement, Axiom deployed an AI-enabled senior lawyer who used Legora to process 344 supplier contracts for a Fortune 10 healthcare company, saving 70% compared to outside counsel costs. Axiom's own 2025 AI study found that only 20% of legal departments achieve AI maturity despite 33% budget increases — a gap Axiom is actively positioning itself to close in the healthcare vertical. The email agent should either receive a post genuinely relevant to legal AI, ALSP trends, or healthcare compliance — or the campaign targeting should be revisited before outreach is sent. If proceeding anyway, a rep could open with: *\"As you're scaling Axiom's AI Tech+Talent offering into healthcare, where do you see the biggest gap between what in-house legal teams say they want from AI and what they're actually ready to adopt?\"*", "event_id": "1565094526", "object_id": "533963448020", "attempt_number": 2, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
