{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-33e51a88b2e24464", "event": "run_summary", "ts": 1787758457.0705745, "trigger_id": null, "events_received": 1, "routed": 1, "discarded": 0, "routing_errors": 0, "discards_by_reason": {}, "dispatched_ok": 0, "dispatched_failed": 1, "duration_ms": 93939.13}
{"stream": "process", "run_id": "run-29e5430ffc864d2d", "event": "routing_decision", "ts": 1787758460.4660788, "trigger_id": "trg-f3d6417114375c93bb693a54", "decision": "route", "agent": "email", "endpoint": "https://uniformly-spongy-unpadded.ngrok-free.dev/email/campaign", "route_id": "R2-lead-context", "property_name": "lead_context", "property_value": "Cedar is a healthcare financial platform that, as of early 2026, is leaning heavily into AI-driven API infrastructure to power its personalization at scale. The company recently announced new AI capabilities, expanding its Cedar Intelligence decision engine to personalize outreach, timing, channel, tone, and resolution options across the billing journey. Cedar's platform unifies billing, payments, coverage, and support into a single solution that continuously learns and adapts, connecting over 200+ healthcare and financial partners. This level of integration means Cedar almost certainly operates a complex, high-volume API layer — exactly the environment where robust FastAPI logging and observability becomes operationally critical. Their 2026 Healthcare Financial Experience Study draws on 1.5 billion patient interactions, which signals the scale at which their backend systems must perform reliably. Logging is critical for understanding and debugging FastAPI apps in production; for APIs, this breaks down into request logs and application logs, which ideally are correlated so each log record is linked to the API request — a directly relevant challenge for a platform processing interactions at Cedar's scale. Our post covers exactly this problem space. A good opening question for the rep: *When Cedar's engineering team is investigating a performance or reliability issue across its patient-facing API layer, what does their current logging and observability workflow look like, and where do the biggest blind spots tend to appear?*", "event_id": "3160878588", "object_id": "533965249249", "attempt_number": 0, "basis": "property + value matched a route in agents_registry.yaml"}
